# Frontend build-time environment.
#
# There is almost nothing here any more, and that is the point. The SPA is
# served by the FastAPI BFF from the same origin and every API call is a
# relative path, so the browser needs no upstream URLs, no GCP project
# identifiers, and no TLS material. All of that now lives in the BFF's own
# environment (see bff/README.md and the plan's §4 configuration contract).
#
# Removed in the Entra BFF restructure:
#   VITE_TRANSLATION_API_ORIGIN      the BFF proxies /api/translation/v1
#   VITE_SALES_API_ORIGIN            the BFF proxies /api/sales/v1
#   VITE_TRANSLATION_CLOUD_RUN_URL   Apigee is the only upstream now
#   VITE_SALES_CLOUD_RUN_URL         "
#   VITE_CONTRACTS_API_BASE          Contract Management page was unrouted, removed
#   VITE_GCP_PROJECT_ID/NUMBER/REGION  the browser no longer talks to GCP
#   VITE_TLS_CA_FILE                 the BFF makes the outbound TLS connection
#   VITE_USE_MOCKS                   mocks live in the BFF (UPSTREAM_MODE=mock)

# Where `npm run dev` proxies /auth and /api. Dev only; not read by the build.
BFF_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8080
